# Pairs with HandOffBound. Moved from the design's
# ReadPositionHonestRestampUnderAnyIntent. Markers are range-scoped, so another
# intent's marker need not cover L: dropping L's marker from the re-stamp's guard
# stands for an open intent disjoint from L, and the re-stamped walk is allocated
# above the head L's closed marker recorded.
MODULE: HandOffBoundRestampUnderAnyIntent
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a rejected walk re-stamps under any open intent, not only its own
PERTURBS: GRestamp

--- FIND
    /\ gst = "rejected"
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ ~closing
    /\ gst' = "repend"
--- REPLACE
    /\ gst = "rejected"
\* MUTATION: any open intent of the tree, not the walk's own.
    /\ ~closing
    /\ gst' = "repend"
--- END
